abstract: >
  A non-LLM, zero-generation developmental system that accumulates a
  continuous individual history. Its inner speech is retrieval over what it
  has heard, so no utterance can be fabricated. Forty-one pre-registered
  experiments and their follow-ups report every outcome, including failures.
  The central finding is negative: the system's workspace is read-only --- its
  thoughts change what it wants and how it represents itself, but cannot
  change its own state. The negative survived six independent escalations,
  including opening the gate and verifying it fired, writing to a consumed
  variable, and raising the coupling to 1.99 sigma. Positive results further
  along the developmental order are reported with their own limits: referential
  grounding, an adaptive vocabulary spurt, word-level composition, and a
  dialogue-state vector. Code is MIT-licensed; the caregiver corpus is derived
  from CHILDES/TalkBank and is not redistributed. Authorship and priority
  evidence are recorded in PROVENANCE.md.
